A bounded request pass and a durable recovery record solve different problems. On HTTP Workers, waitUntil extends execution for up to 30 seconds after response or disconnect; that allowance is shared.

Book basis: [B4](/lore/durability-bibliography#b4-release-it), [B6](/lore/durability-bibliography#b6-fundamentals-of-data-engineering).

## Failure it prevents

Three 20-second attempts plus delays need more time than the post-response allowance, so background delivery is cut off without recovery.

## Our Effect 4.0.0 reading

Use one deadline for the pass and cap every attempt at remaining time. `Context.Reference` can hold an intentional default budget. Do not cache an absolute deadline in it. Persist an undelivered marker for independent redrive.

Source: `packages/effect/src/Context.ts`, `packages/effect/src/Effect.ts`.

## How to check

Use a 25-second example budget. Cancel post-response work, then redrive the persisted marker with the same operation identity and prove duplicate safety. This check is our proposal. The books do not prescribe it.

Continue with [Timeouts bound waiting](/lore/timeouts-bound-waiting), [Retry needs idempotent effects](/lore/retry-needs-idempotency).

